![high](https://www.gstatic.com/codereviewagent/high-priority.svg)

If parallel tool calls are interleaved or sent in the same chunk, and the provider repeats the `id` on subsequent chunks, comparing only against `accumulated[latest].id` will fail. For example, if we have two active tool calls (index 0 for `call_a` and index 1 for `call_b`), a subsequent chunk for `call_a` will have `latest = 1` (which is `call_b`). Comparing `call_a` to `call_b` will result in `starts_new_call = True`, incorrectly starting a third tool call (index 2) instead of continuing index 0.

By looking up the `id` across all accumulated tool calls, we can correctly route the fragment to the existing slot regardless of the order or interleaving of chunks.

```suggestion
    if tool_call.id:
        for k, v in accumulated.items():
            if getattr(v, 'id', None) == tool_call.id:
                return k
        starts_new_call = True
    else:
        starts_new_call = bool(tool_call.function and tool_call.function.name)
    return latest + 1 if starts_new_call else latest
```
